          {
            "title": "Fencing Target Robot",
            "meta": "Elite Fencing Club",
            "badge": "",
            "body": "- Currently building a Robot to train reaction time and aim for foil fencing. When a target area glows, the trainee is supposed to hit that area and get an average reaction time at the end of their session.\n- While Favero is my biggest competitor in the market, I believe I can produce a cheaper alternative with a humanoid shape and more versatile features.\n- To protect the target's LEDs, I created custom hard-plastic molds to withstand up to 800 N of force over an area of 38.5 mm².\n- I am adding more sections to give trainees more variation in where to attack.\n- Eventually, I would like to add wheels and possibly a robotic arm to the training dummy to show how a given defense might expose different body sections.",
            "tags": [
              "Arduino",
              "C++",
              "Electrical Engineering",
              "SWOT Analysis",
              "Circuit Design",
              "3-D Printing",
              "OnShape",
              "Mold Making",
              "Epoxy Resin Casting"
            ],
