            "title": "Intergroup Conflict Calculator",
            "meta": "Computer Science",
            "badge": "Pending Publication",
            "body": "- Identified a gap in quantitative conflict-prediction methodology. Specificcally built on the Realistic Conflict Theory by Muzafer Sharif.\n- Engineered a scalable mathematical framework drawing on 11 Social Psychological theories to compute conflict likelihood between two groups as a probabilistic output.\n- Architected a full-stack React web app (HTML, CSS, Firebase) exposing the model as an interactive calculator.\n- Deployed on Firebase Hosting with a Firestore-backed logging layer for usage analytics.",
